<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
        V1 BASELINE for the PAYMENTS report generator in dcre_pay (owner directive
        2026-08-08: every DCRE database is dropped and cut over directly, so there is
        no historic state to migrate and no deployed schema to protect).

        This is NOT a port of CRG's 53-changeset history. Each object is declared once
        in its final shape, and the re-run guards that history required are absent on
        purpose. DATABASECHANGELOG is what makes a re-run safe from a clean baseline;
        the guards CRG carries (validCheckSum ANY on designed schema, MARK_RAN
        preconditions over pre-existing objects, IF-NOT-EXISTS on CREATEs) existed to
        survive a migration that has now been abandoned, and reproducing them would be
        exactly the hacking-around-Liquibase the owner has forbidden.

        Two deliberate exceptions, both of which are live requirements rather than
        history:
          - 001 guards tables PRG does NOT own with onFail="CONTINUE". PRG is
            clock-launched and can migrate before PRR/PTV/PRW/PIX/PSX/PPX have ever
            run, and CREATE VIEW against an absent table crash-loops the pod.
          - 004 vendors Spring Batch's own framework DDL, which is multi-statement,
            non-transactional on CockroachDB, and therefore genuinely needs
            IF NOT EXISTS to survive a mid-migration kill.

        Order is load-bearing: sources, then owned tables (the views reference
        prg_status_class and prg_delivery_ledger), then views, then batch metadata.
    -->
    <include file="db/changelog/2026/08/001-pay-report-sources.xml"/>
    <include file="db/changelog/2026/08/002-pay-reporting.xml"/>
    <include file="db/changelog/2026/08/003-pay-status-views.xml"/>
    <include file="db/changelog/2026/08/004-batch-metadata.xml"/>

</databaseChangeLog>
